{
  "repository": "sv5byp/FTFlow",
  "tag": "r150",
  "title": "FTflow r150 - Portable Windows x64",
  "body": "FTflow r150 is portable Windows x64 software for weak-signal digital communication on amateur radio bands, based on MSHV.\n\nDownload **FTflow-SV5BYP-r150-Windows-x64-portable.zip**, extract the complete ZIP into a folder on your hard disk and run **FTFlow.exe**. **No setup or installer is required.** It can also run from a USB stick. Keep all included files and subfolders together.\n\nFor an existing installation, use **Help > Check for updates**. For a manual upgrade, close FTflow, retain a backup and copy **FTFlow.exe** and **FTFlow-Update.exe** into the existing permanent folder. Keep your settings and logs.\n\nThe source ZIP is for developers. FTFlow-update.bin and FTFlow-update.sig are used by the built-in updater. Ordinary users should download the Windows x64 portable ZIP.\n\nBased on MSHV, developed by Hrisimir Hristov, LZ2HV. Original contributor credits, map attribution and the GNU GPL license are retained.\n",
